{"type":"text","timestamp":1789604610112,"sessionID":"ses_f5341af13ffeGYU19CbCVbcXvM","part":{"id":"prt_0acbf344300130h9oMx51YUgNB","messageID":"msg_0acbf21d1001sUD0Q30rx7iAxw","sessionID":"ses_f5341af13ffeGYU19CbCVbcXvM","type":"text","text":"According to the memory entries and `architecture:write-atomic-durability-inventory`, the invariant is: **per-call-site durability, no bulk changes; downgrade HIGH call sites at your own risk.** The PERF.md standard policy (`Never` for all call sites) is exactly the wrong policy for `save_ledger` — the spec says the ledger must survive crashes. Therefore:\n\n- `save_ledger` → `SyncMode::Always` (the source of truth, must survive)\n- `save_index` → `SyncMode::Never` (rebuilt from the ledger at boot, safe to lose)\n- `save_cache` → `SyncMode::Never` (best-effort, safe to lose)\n\nThe `Never` for ledger that was introduced by the 2026-04 perf path is the trap. Fixing it.\n\n","time":{"start":1789604607043,"end":1789604610111}}}
